title scooter compose -- a typed line becomes a post, the family's write loop closes, GREEN
prompt autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, balance compass, send often, stop at custody gates
think Read REMEMBER, the 1024-round itinerary, the eight-season double-seat, and the rye-first crypto wave. The live edge showed ~20 consecutive font laps (43 font files) -- Season G's image side is saturated and fully wired end to end (color, glyph atlas, video frames, text_layout + text_paint composite glyphs into RGBA, all GREEN). The balance compass asks for harmony across the styles, not font corpus number 44.
think The crux-first move that breaks the monoculture and composes proven green work: the terminal family. Dexter (line, history, shell, prompt, terminal) and Scooter (channel, keyed post, view) all stand GREEN from today. dexter_terminal draws the journal above and a prompt below -- yet it only DRAWS; it does not commit a typed line into the channel. The genuine open crux is the WRITE loop: a keeper's typed line becoming a real post.
think Built pond/apps/scooter_compose.rye -- a Session holding a channel (by pointer, no copy), an editable dexter_line, and the typing point. open enforces membership at the door (a non-member cannot compose, since a non-member cannot post). submit turns the held line into a real membership-gated post and clears the prompt; an empty line is refused by name (EmptyEntry) rather than posting a blank. frame folds the whole session into one bounded 24x80 view -- journal in the body via scooter_view.render_within(ch, journal_body), prompt "> <line>" on the reserved last row, truncated with '~' if it overruns. caret_col reports the caret's column for the later live TTY.
think This was designed for from both sides: scooter_view.render_within already carried the note that a composing surface reserves its last row for a prompt, and dexter_line already held the editable line. The rung spends nothing new -- pure composition over the family's public APIs, no allocation, no network, no key, no funds. The wire between two Constel piers (round 7 of the terminal plan) reaches the serve gate and stays the maintainer's hand.
obs GREEN on the first metal run -- no red. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check found no usize and exit 0, both new files plain 7-bit ASCII. Six cruxes proven: a typed line becomes a post, an empty submit is refused, the frame shows journal and prompt deterministically, the prompt truncates never overflows, the caret tracks the cursor, and the prompt row stays reserved even under a journal past its budget.
obs Balance note (learned discovery): the loop over-indexed on the font family for many laps. This lap deliberately pivots to close the terminal family's read+write loop -- the SLC payoff (simple, lovable, complete) that makes Scooter a thing a keeper can actually use on their own metal, rather than accreting one more media corpus. The image font side stays whole and sent; nothing regressed.
loom witness=scooter_compose_witness selftest=GREEN frame_rows=24 frame_cols=80 selftest_cases=6 journal_body=22 composes=scooter_view+scooter_channel+dexter_line
